==Enemy==
Although Calamary's health, attack damage and movement speed aren't too high, she has long range and the ability to [[weaken]] cats to 10% of their normal attack power. She only has one knockback, so she can't reposition unless one uses [[:Category:Cats with Knockback ability|cats with knockback abilities]].

==Strategy==
If you have [[:Category:Cats with Weaken Immunity|units with Weaken Immunity]], units that have higher range than her, [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|wave attackers]], or [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance Cats]] with enough piercing range to snipe her, then Calamary will be a lot easier to defeat. [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Radiant Aphrodite]], [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Li'l Nyandam]] and Cyborg Cat are some examples.

As long as there's at least one enemy at the frontlines, [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]] will be highly effective, as the [[Wave Attack|waves]] resulting from his attack will reach Calamary and deal moderate damage. [[Akira (Uber Rare Cat)|Akira]] can be super useful against her as he has anti-Alien abilities (Normal/[[True Form]]) and cannot be weakened.

If you have no units that outrange Calamary and your wave attackers are not cutting it, use tanky cats like [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera]]/[[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed M. Titan Cat]]. Units with fast movement speed such as [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Sanada Yukimura]]/[[Count Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Count Yukimura]] or [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] can also be used, as they can possibly evade Calamary's ability and deal huge damage to her if timed correctly.

