==Trivia==
*Going off of the shape of her head and the length and positioning of her tentacles, Calamary appears to be based on the species ''[[wikipedia:Loligo vulgaris|Loligo vulgaris]]'', commonly known as the European squid (''calamary'', plural ''calamaries'', is an uncommon synonym of squid, used particularly for those in the genus ''Loligo''; ''calamari'' is a different word and the culinary term for squid'').
**Since her Japanese description calls her a true Tokyoite, another species she could be based on is the [[wikipedia:Japanese flying squid|Japanese flying squid]], which also matches Calamary's silhouette fairly well and would explain her [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] trait.
*Her translucency may be a reference to [[wikipedia:Glass squid|glass squids]], most of which live up to their namesake.
*Her Japanese namesake is [http://www.yotchan.co.jp/ Yotchan], a brand of dried squid snacks.
*In [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]], Calamary's catchphrase is "Attarimē yo!" (あったりめーよ！), which would mean something like, "It's only natural!" The joke is that it sounds similar to ''atarime'' (当たりめ), meaning dried cuttlefish.
*The fish market mentioned in her description is a [[wikipedia:Tsukiji fish market|real place]].


